/-!
# QUBIT-TRADE VI: the sample criterion is a generation criterion in `ZMod r`

The arithmetic criterion of `SampleFungibility.lean` — a record of Shor samples
`k₁, …, k_m` recovers the order `r` iff `gcd (gcd_i k_i, r) = 1` — is exactly a
*group-theoretic* statement about the cyclic group `ZMod r`:

  **a record recovers the order iff the sampled numerators generate `ZMod r`.**

* `QubitTrade.recovered_eq_addOrderOf` — one sample returns the additive order of
  `k` in `ZMod r`, i.e. the size of the subgroup it generates;
* `QubitTrade.recordGcd_mem_closure` — the joint gcd of a record lies in the
  subgroup generated by the record (Bézout, by induction along the list);
* `QubitTrade.closure_eq_top_iff_gcd` — the generation criterion;
* `QubitTrade.samples_recover_iff_generate` — the bridge: `recordEstimate ks r = r`
  iff the samples generate `ZMod r`.

So "qubit ↔ sample fungibility" is the statement that extra samples enlarge the
subgroup of `ZMod r` that the algorithm has seen, until it is everything; while
extra qubits (below the resolution threshold) enlarge nothing at all.
-/

open QubitTrade

theorem QubitTrade.recordGcd_mem_closure(ks : List ℕ) (r : ℕ) :
    ((recordGcd ks : ℕ) : ZMod r) ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (recordImage ks r) := by sorry
